* Rename resources/abi-dumps to resources/compat-dumps or similar. (see
  below)

* Change wording throughout to "compatibility check" or "compat check" vs
  "ABI check", "ABI dump", "compliance check" etc. Despite its name,
  abi-compliance-checker checks source level compatibility in addition to
  binary compatibility. And "compliance" is less precise than
  "compatibility".

* Rename compat-check2!

* Deduplicate dump generation code - either consolidate generate/check into
  one script or use a library.

* Remove bespoke compat check script, data

* Fix abi-compliance-checker binary compat check for ppc64le: no symbols
  detected, ABI breaks go undetected. The builds for other arches detect
  problems correctly, so the risk isn't exactly high, but ppc64le is our
  primary target. This is due to 'readelf -Ws' producing '[<localentry>: x]'
  strings in its output for ppc64le objects. See:
  * https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20191201195728.4161537-1-aurelien@aurel32.net/
  * https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1479302
  Options? Fix abi-compliance-checker with a local patch, or a wrapper
  script around readelf to filter out the confusing strings.

* Evaluate "-strict" option for abi-compliance-checker.

* Evaluate "-show-retval" option for abi-compliance-checker. (show symbol
  return type)

* Add useful version information to compat reports. Right now they say
  "between X and X" (literally).

* CI: Build with more compilers/versions.

* CI: Remove 'file .libs/librtas.so*' from distcheck step
